01:05:09,512 --> 01:05:12,478
David Budaya has pulled up a little bit as well.

643
01:05:12,538 --> 01:05:14,460
Tom Daley up to 15th.

644
01:05:14,541 --> 01:05:28,784
He might have to come out of the pack as it were to try to get into a good position rather like running a 10k out there on the track not too far away where you get through those qualifying rounds in shape and look to build.

645
01:05:29,125 --> 01:05:36,297
That's certainly what the crowd in this fantastic 17,000-seater Aquatic Centre will be hoping

646
01:05:36,277 --> 01:05:44,893
Down there on that caption, these are the ones who really are just wanting to be back here in the morning and to make their Olympic Games more than a six dive wonder.

647
01:05:44,974 --> 01:05:48,902
Peter Waterfield there, the other home favourite with a huge amount of work to do.

648
01:05:49,456 --> 01:06:17,757
Matthew Mitchum also on the bubble sitting in the sixteenth position so he can't afford to have things go wrong but Cleb Galperin has made a very good start two excellent dives that would probably be the worst of his three Galperin was first after the first rotation second after the second forward three and a half somersault there for the Olympic Games bronze medalist in Beijing

649
01:06:20,657 --> 01:06:21,860
Didn't make the synchro team.

650
01:06:21,880 --> 01:06:27,286
And just a 66 for his third drive.

651
01:06:27,327 --> 01:06:31,672
That's a disappointing one for Galperin.

652
01:06:31,692 --> 01:06:41,465
Interestingly enough, neither of China's gold medal winning 10 meter synchro team actually made the individual competition, which is just astonishing.

653
01:06:41,485 --> 01:06:42,126
Lin Yue.

654
01:06:43,878 --> 01:06:45,900
Oh goodness me.

655
01:06:46,480 --> 01:06:50,764
Back three and a half somersault there and he's starting to show his pedigree I think.

656
01:06:51,043 --> 01:06:54,007
And now we're seeing why they come to this event as favorites.

657
01:06:58,409 --> 01:06:59,570
What a position he adopts.

658
01:07:00,072 --> 01:07:03,173
What an entry he achieves and what splash.

659
01:07:04,976 --> 01:07:06,356
Slicing into the water there.

660
01:07:07,137 --> 01:07:08,358
Look how tight he is there.

661
01:07:08,398 --> 01:07:10,000
Really hugging those legs.

662
01:07:11,240 --> 01:07:13,242
That's enormous flexibility.

663
01:07:16,936 --> 01:07:17,717
They're not just slim.

664
01:07:17,757 --> 01:07:25,213
Look at the power and the muscle definition on his thighs and the push-up and the stomach muscle strength to pull out of those dives.

665
01:07:26,135 --> 01:07:27,498
There's a 100-point dive.

666
01:07:33,791 --> 01:07:36,496
Victor Ortega from Colombia.

667
01:07:39,193 --> 01:07:44,043
previously competed at the Olympics in the synchro event.

668
01:07:45,125 --> 01:07:49,873
Arm stand back triple somersault, tucked.

669
01:07:49,893 --> 01:07:50,514
No respectable.

670
01:07:52,378 --> 01:07:58,409
He's in 25th after the second dive so he's fighting to be back tomorrow morning.

671
01:08:00,813 --> 01:08:02,737
Just didn't really control the entry.

672
01:08:08,000 --> 01:08:12,907
He's got three more dives to try and consolidate his position.

673
01:08:20,659 --> 01:08:26,970
Anton Zakharov just missed out in a synchro medal back in 2004 at the Olympic Games.

674
01:08:29,346 --> 01:08:37,840
Well, those high speed forward, four and a half somersaults tucked with a 3.7 tariff, if you nail it.

675
01:08:37,859 --> 01:08:42,907
Well, it always looked like he did have it in control, not too horizontal with his takeoff from the platform.

676
01:08:44,009 --> 01:08:47,673
The ankle's just slightly apart, made a good job of the entry.

677
01:08:50,097 --> 01:08:54,083
Some from column A, some from column B, as we say.

678
01:08:54,104 --> 01:08:56,367
And he's got his little support crew here.

679
01:08:58,877 --> 01:09:02,141
certainly tell the Ukrainians in that very distinctive kit they wear.

680
01:09:02,783 --> 01:09:03,703
Spot them a mile off.

681
01:09:04,083 --> 01:09:08,930
Anything in the 80s you'll take and he's had 72 and 88 and an 83.

682
01:09:10,371 --> 01:09:18,440
Timofey Odechik he was right down in 30th position forward three and a half some assaults was the intention there.

683
01:09:19,101 --> 01:09:20,103
He's come up short hasn't he?

684
01:09:20,443 --> 01:09:21,864
Never got through it.

685
01:09:23,206 --> 01:09:28,091
He's just struggling to reach his best in this competition and

686
01:09:32,087 --> 01:09:36,305
See his head well away from the knees compared to our two Chinese stars.

687
01:09:37,773 --> 01:09:38,716
Just a different position.

688
01:09:38,796 --> 01:09:41,710
He can still make that work but he didn't on that occasion.

689
01:09:46,229 --> 01:09:53,099
There on that 10 meter board from the Democratic People's Republic of Korea.

690
01:09:53,238 --> 01:09:55,082
Just 16 years of age.

691
01:09:56,184 --> 01:09:58,546
Arm stand back, triple somersault.

692
01:09:58,567 --> 01:10:04,275
Now, how quickly will he be into the dive from his hold position?

693
01:10:06,059 --> 01:10:06,800
Up very quickly.

694
01:10:06,819 --> 01:10:08,322
Oh, he's not got it there.

695
01:10:09,854 --> 01:10:34,747
he can do it again but there is a there's a time on this and more than anything else this is a major test good luck well he had to hurry that to get into the position again and and a reminder of just how big that part of the dive is a test and not just to be taken for granted what they're doing before they even set off

696
01:10:35,251 --> 01:10:47,243
So he had to rush it in the end and under some pressure he's flopped over, over rotated, big splash and it will be a difficult dive to come back from.

697
01:10:47,283 --> 01:10:58,997
The feeling of panic when you lose that then when it is all about composure at the top of that board must be absolutely unimaginable.

698
01:11:01,711 --> 01:11:03,372
So he's really been punished there.

699
01:11:03,934 --> 01:11:05,034
The score of eighteen.

700
01:11:06,997 --> 01:11:08,520
That is that's crippling.

701
01:11:08,560 --> 01:11:10,743
That is that's awful.

702
01:11:10,762 --> 01:11:13,126
Jimmy Connor, seventeen-year-old Australian.

703
01:11:14,587 --> 01:11:15,829
In with three and a half somersaults.

704
01:11:16,810 --> 01:11:17,992
Back in twenty-fourth.

705
01:11:20,055 --> 01:11:29,186
Needs to put on a bit of a show here if he's going to be back in the morning or else he could be having a late night

706
01:11:32,930 --> 01:11:56,929
Well, I was concerned for him because he seemed to be there an age convincing himself when to go and yet he's done a good job here.

707
01:11:57,887 --> 01:12:04,176
Must be almost like getting the yips, you know, golfers and even they call it dartitis in darts when you can't let go.

708
01:12:04,216 --> 01:12:10,505
He's got it right in the end.

709
01:12:10,545 --> 01:12:11,806
Well played.

710
01:12:14,289 --> 01:12:17,033
Give some concession to his youth here, one of the younger divers at 17.

711
01:12:17,054 --> 01:12:20,097
76.8.

712
01:12:22,828 --> 01:12:25,332
So one in the mid 60s and two in the high 70s.

713
01:12:25,953 --> 01:12:26,875
He's hanging around there.

714
01:12:27,735 --> 01:12:29,578
Martin Vulfrom from Germany.

715
01:12:31,921 --> 01:12:35,648
He was here in February in the World Cup, finished ninth at this height.

716
01:12:36,890 --> 01:12:41,015
Reverse three and a half somersault.

717
01:12:41,036 --> 01:12:41,676
Oh, good job.

718
01:12:41,697 --> 01:12:44,962
And he was 19th after the second dive.

719
01:12:45,802 --> 01:12:48,006
So he too is right on that cut.

720
01:12:49,769 --> 01:12:52,632
This needed to be as good as it turned out to be.

721
01:12:53,997 --> 01:12:55,298
This is a wonderful entry.

722
01:12:56,742 --> 01:13:00,408
Martin Wolfram has really surged up the standings with this one.

723
01:13:08,903 --> 01:13:12,208
Not sure how much of that lack of a square position the judges will see.

724
01:13:12,269 --> 01:13:16,435
They haven't punished him for it really with an 87-4-5, some nines in there.

725
01:13:16,856 --> 01:13:17,557
That's a great effort.

726
01:13:19,377 --> 01:13:21,279
from Cuba.

727
01:13:22,240 --> 01:13:24,265
Back three and a half somersault.

728
01:13:25,386 --> 01:13:28,131
He's down twenty-second position.

729
01:13:28,230 --> 01:13:30,994
So, it's within range.

730
01:13:31,636 --> 01:13:39,207
The difficulty here is three point six for the back three and a half somersault.

731
01:13:43,997 --> 01:13:55,994
Well, didn't quite get there and this was his highest tariff dive or he's got another one coming for his last that's also 3.6 but these are the ones you really need to make most use of.

732
01:13:57,757 --> 01:14:11,537
He'd gone to the semi-final in last year's World Championship so he would have probably come to London expecting at least to come back for a second round of dives but this is the world's best.

733
01:14:11,637 --> 01:14:12,840
It's going to be difficult.

734
01:14:14,878 --> 01:14:16,400
and a big splash on entry.

735
01:14:16,461 --> 01:14:19,466
Therefore, and a sixty-four point eight.

736
01:14:20,547 --> 01:14:21,309
That won't help him.

737
01:14:24,975 --> 01:14:33,507
Ukrainian Alexander Bondar, eighteen-year-old from Lugansk with a arm stand back double somersault two and a half twist.

738
01:14:34,909 --> 01:14:36,311
I mean, he's up in sixth place.

739
01:14:36,752 --> 01:14:43,063
Needs to just get that

740
01:14:48,729 --> 01:14:49,372
Still there.

741
01:14:55,007 --> 01:14:58,256
No.

742
01:14:58,277 --> 01:15:03,010
Has to take something out of the shoulders being in that position that long.

743
01:15:05,368 --> 01:15:10,118
seemed to be almost too keen to get into the twist before he'd really got himself away from the board.

744
01:15:10,417 --> 01:15:19,734
Yeah and he was bent at the hips, bad position entering the water, the ankles came apart also so there was some leg form issues throughout the dive.

745
01:15:21,618 --> 01:15:29,131
They only came together at the end but the entry was not too special so a 57.6 and Bondar is going to plummet down the rankings.

746
01:15:32,908 --> 01:15:34,970
went all said and done after the third.

747
01:15:35,731 --> 01:15:40,497
Consistency, that's the big test across six dives.

748
01:15:42,801 --> 01:15:45,623
Ki-hoo Park from Korea, 20 year old.

749
01:15:47,966 --> 01:15:49,148
Back three and a half somersault.

750
01:15:51,890 --> 01:15:54,253
Oh and he's overdone that one as well.

751
01:15:55,255 --> 01:15:57,537
He's struggling really, Park.

752
01:15:59,260 --> 01:16:00,081
Not his night.

753
01:16:03,166 --> 01:16:08,971
It must be so hard to put the previous dive behind you and start from scratch every time.

754
01:16:09,011 --> 01:16:18,180
It's a bit like a golfer stepping up on the tee again after a double bogey and needing to clear all the negatives out and starting again with each dive.

755
01:16:18,440 --> 01:16:21,043
He just never got into a really tight tuck position.

756
01:16:21,604 --> 01:16:25,188
Even the split tuck would have helped him get through those rotations more quickly.

757
01:16:26,109 --> 01:16:28,430
So some technique issues there for Park.

758
01:16:32,426 --> 01:16:34,029
Victor Mini Vive.

759
01:16:38,819 --> 01:16:40,922
Synchro partner of Ilya Zakharov.

760
01:16:48,136 --> 01:16:51,162
Reverse three and a half somersault another long wait at the top there.

761
01:16:57,301 --> 01:16:58,021
Very nice.

762
01:16:58,261 --> 01:16:59,863
Eleventh after two dives.

763
01:17:00,503 --> 01:17:02,447
I don't think he's going to give up any ground with that one.

764
01:17:04,969 --> 01:17:06,711
Half an arm movement at the top there.

765
01:17:06,751 --> 01:17:10,654
It looked as though he wasn't quite sure and then he was all very positive.

766
01:17:14,458 --> 01:17:15,820
Judges are fairly happy with it.

767
01:17:16,140 --> 01:17:21,587
The feet just rolled over at the very end but very positive entry.

768
01:17:23,069 --> 01:17:37,095
and Nivaev after a rough start a 67 with his first dive 86.95 is second and then 82.5 for his third so starting to produce it

769
01:17:38,273 --> 01:17:45,065
Next up, it's twenty-year-old German Sanchez from Guadalajara in Mexico who's having an excellent games.

770
01:17:45,086 --> 01:17:47,710
The silver medal from the Syncro already in his kit.

771
01:17:48,511 --> 01:17:50,796
And it's third after two dives.

772
01:17:51,637 --> 01:17:54,582
And now with an arm stand back, triple somersault.

773
01:17:55,966 --> 01:17:58,289
How long will it take him to get into that key position?

774
01:18:00,634 --> 01:18:02,037
Legs wide and closing.

775
01:18:09,728 --> 01:18:15,242
Well, he looked more confident at the top than he did at the bottom, where the entry was less than ideal.

776
01:18:15,301 --> 01:18:26,690
He's got a little bit of room to play with, having come into this series well positioned.

777
01:18:31,987 --> 01:18:35,070
former junior world silver medalist at 10 meters.

778
01:18:35,771 --> 01:18:41,819
That was only in 2010, so they are so young, these competitors, many of them.

779
01:18:42,539 --> 01:18:46,284
Father's a professional footballer, so he should know a little bit about diving.

780
01:18:46,305 --> 01:18:49,628
There's one or two footballers one could say that they've dived a little bit.

781
01:18:49,810 --> 01:18:51,190
That's unkind, right?

782
01:18:51,211 --> 01:18:52,432
That's well worked in, though.

783
01:18:52,472 --> 01:18:53,033
Nice segue.

784
01:18:53,354 --> 01:18:59,681
Seventy, seventy five point nine for his third as we move on to Riley McCormick from Canada.

785
01:19:03,965 --> 01:19:15,041
14th in with three and a half somersault.

786
01:19:15,060 --> 01:19:21,871
Lovely that McCormick will be proud of that one I think especially the entry.

787
01:19:26,597 --> 01:19:29,162
This is a zero splash dive if you like.

788
01:19:30,880 --> 01:19:35,904
He just pulls that water down with him, the air that he's created, the arms separate.

789
01:19:36,845 --> 01:19:46,117
There's a bit of a technique to this, to ripping the entry, and he's giving him 9 out of 10 for the entry, not that they separate them, but, you know, sitting up here we can.

790
01:19:47,198 --> 01:19:47,818
And an 80.

791
01:19:48,899 --> 01:19:54,845
From Arizona State University, combining his diving with his studies in the United States.

792
01:19:55,905 --> 01:19:58,028
He wants our job, a career in broadcasting.

793
01:19:59,208 --> 01:20:00,530
Matthew Mitchum.

794
01:20:00,551 --> 01:20:02,492
I think he needs to make a statement now, Mitchum.

795
01:20:02,773 --> 01:20:05,354
He's just had a pedestrian couple of first two dives.

796
01:20:07,396 --> 01:20:10,520
Him with three and a half somersault for the defending champion.

797
01:20:13,984 --> 01:20:14,463
That's better.

798
01:20:16,485 --> 01:20:25,574
Well, the evidence shows that he knows how to pull out the big one on the big occasion, but he has left himself a little bit more work than he would have expected.

799
01:20:28,728 --> 01:20:57,333
very good entry and he's going to pull some eights and a very split tuck position but then pulls it back together again for the entry competed in the three meter springboard at the last Olympics didn't qualify for the final but now concentrating and he's got a mark in the 80s to perhaps move him up the rankings we'll see when everyone's finished three

800
01:20:58,680 --> 01:21:00,761
Back three and a half somersault.

801
01:21:00,780 --> 01:21:01,467
He's 12th.

802
01:21:10,493 --> 01:21:16,381
competed at one metre in the World Championships, one metre of course not an Olympic event.

803
01:21:18,565 --> 01:21:26,679
His problem there was that even in the tuck position his feet weren't aligned and the judges side on would have been able to see that as perhaps you did too.

804
01:21:28,081 --> 01:21:29,524
That's an unusual error really.

805
01:21:29,564 --> 01:21:37,176
And the 64-3 fire for Gizmovic.

806
01:21:42,269 --> 01:21:44,453
Looks to be good camaraderie around the pool.

807
01:21:45,194 --> 01:21:49,319
We love seeing that at the Olympics, even at the very top level, that the athletes are friends.

808
01:21:50,341 --> 01:21:54,269
We've seen plenty of that in all the sports across the games, which has been great.

809
01:21:54,569 --> 01:22:02,761
Francesco De Luomo, because it's a lonely place at the top of that board, in with three and a half somersault.

810
01:22:05,546 --> 01:22:06,268
Very good.

811
01:22:07,176 --> 01:22:09,460
Francesco will come up smiling.

812
01:22:09,479 --> 01:22:13,185
You sometimes get a sense of how the diver feels about it, how quickly they come to the surface.

813
01:22:13,204 --> 01:22:14,506
Well, I hear some of this applause.

814
01:22:14,546 --> 01:22:15,407
I thought that went all right.

815
01:22:15,447 --> 01:22:16,287
What's the crowd think?

816
01:22:16,929 --> 01:22:17,649
Well, they liked it.

817
01:22:20,514 --> 01:22:23,497
He was a European silver medalist back in 2004.

818
01:22:24,198 --> 01:22:30,105
So he's had a good length career to know how to deal with these occasions.

819
01:22:31,707 --> 01:22:33,369
An eighty one six.

820
01:22:37,737 --> 01:22:56,936
Christopher Eskilsson from Sweden who's been doing too badly at 12 equal after three dives and now an arm stand back triple somersault.

821
01:22:56,957 --> 01:23:06,867
Well he executed the dive okay but he didn't look convincing in the handstand he once he reached a position where he felt confident he did move but he hadn't held it for long

822
01:23:11,807 --> 01:23:13,399
Judges aren't too unhappy with him.

823
01:23:13,439 --> 01:23:18,391
He was pretty vertical for the entry, even if it wasn't a low splash affair.

824
01:23:26,707 --> 01:23:28,711
And a seventy-two point six.

825
01:23:30,894 --> 01:23:38,944
These the boys that are sort of on the bubble, it brings its own pressure when you get about halfway through the competition, you realize that you can't muck up a dive.

826
01:23:39,005 --> 01:23:49,979
Eric Sainz said it was a dream come true just to be at the Olympics and admitted that he'd set his stall out to get to the final was his ambition, but he's got some work to do.

827
01:23:51,082 --> 01:23:53,564
Armstand back double somersault, two and a half twist.

828
01:23:54,126 --> 01:23:55,568
He's back in twenty-ninth.

829
01:23:59,108 --> 01:24:00,649
Oh dear, that was short.

830
01:24:00,850 --> 01:24:02,311
He almost fell off the platform.

831
01:24:02,332 --> 01:24:07,019
He's had a couple of poor dives, only three competitors below him.

832
01:24:07,059 --> 01:24:09,841
And I just wonder what's going on here for Eric.

833
01:24:09,881 --> 01:24:11,083
He's a better diver than this.

834
01:24:12,506 --> 01:24:19,395
Well, he'll look at that, as I'm sure he will, and realize that he can do better.

835
01:24:19,762 --> 01:24:24,109
Canadian champion at the individual and the synchro events.

836
01:24:25,471 --> 01:24:33,404
Picked up medals, Pan American Games, Commonwealth Games, but this is a big step up, the Olympic Games.

837
01:24:33,864 --> 01:24:37,310
And a fifty-five point eight for Eric.

838
01:24:37,329 --> 01:24:39,172
He's going to be disheartened by that.

839
01:24:43,573 --> 01:24:45,676
Brian Lomas from Malaysia.

840
01:24:47,579 --> 01:24:53,969
Trains in China where facilities you won't be surprised to discover are top quality.

841
01:24:54,949 --> 01:24:56,112
Back three and a half somersault.

842
01:24:59,877 --> 01:25:05,886
Oh well that's seriously overcooking a fairly straightforward dive.

843
01:25:07,452 --> 01:25:08,894
That's a shame for him.

844
01:25:10,034 --> 01:25:15,041
The crowd reaction told you everything there, let alone what the judges will make of it.

845
01:25:15,081 --> 01:25:18,184
Just tumbling into it like a chimney being demolished.

846
01:25:21,347 --> 01:25:22,828
Yeah, that's a 29.7.

847
01:25:24,030 --> 01:25:28,515
Such a low score that it could be hard to recover from with three dives to come.

848
01:25:29,856 --> 01:25:33,020
And he too is better than that, if you look at his past record.

849
01:25:34,250 --> 01:25:38,436
Now the Mexicans are on a bit of a charge in this diving competition.

850
01:25:40,720 --> 01:25:42,582
Ivan Garcia, fifth.

851
01:25:45,768 --> 01:25:47,251
The Synchro Silver Medalist.

852
01:25:48,733 --> 01:25:51,277
Pan-American double champion.

853
01:25:53,140 --> 01:25:54,601
Seventh at the Worlds last year.

854
01:25:56,125 --> 01:25:57,868
This is a competition that he's familiar with.

855
01:25:58,948 --> 01:26:00,612
A standard he can match.

856
01:26:01,942 --> 01:26:12,069
still only 18 so he is obviously progressing in his career the inward four and a half somersault tucked 4.1 the tariff here a big one

857
01:26:20,420 --> 01:26:23,002
Well, OK.

858
01:26:24,265 --> 01:26:30,051
But when you've got that big tariff, you really are looking to play your joker, as they say, and get the almost the double points.

